# What NOT to upload when deploying this folder directly.
#
# The working folder is 1.7 GB; a deploy needs about 25 MB of it. Everything
# below is either rebuilt on the platform, or is source data the running site
# never reads.

# Rebuilt remotely — and node_modules is platform-specific, so uploading a
# macOS build to a Linux runtime breaks native modules.
node_modules
.next

# The crawl cache: 489 MB of raw YouTube API responses. Only the ingest
# scripts read it, never the site. This is the single biggest upload trap.
data/.ingest-cache.jsonl

# 112 MB uncompressed archive. archive.ts prefers it locally but falls back to
# index.json.gz (20 MB), which is what ships.
data/index.json

# 46 MB precomputed search index, regenerated by the `prebuild` hook during the
# platform's build. Uploading it would also risk shipping a stale one.
data/search-index.bin

# Extraction diagnostics and backfill working files — never read at runtime.
data/unmatched.json
data/noplace-sample.csv
data/backfill
data/audit

.git
.env.local
*.log
